###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Inference times for energy and forces of single molecules on an NVIDIA
# GeForce RTX 4090 (Table 6): TensorNet 1L/2L take 22.1/26.5 ms for alanine
# dipeptide (22 atoms), 22.5/26.9 ms for chignolin (166), 66.9/106.7 ms for
# DHFR (2,489) and 149.8/248.6 ms for Factor IX (5,807). These timings are of
# the 1L and 2L architectures on systems with no accuracy result; they are
# held in the encoding input (linked to the rMD17 aspirin models, whose
# architecture the paper does not say was the one timed). Training speed on
# ANI1x is given in batch steps per second (Table 7).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - TensorNet is implemented within the TorchMD-NET framework but is introduced as a new architecture; no derivation from a registry method is stated.
# - Only U0 of the four QM9 energy targets is encoded (U 3.9, H 4.0, G 5.7 meV are not).
# - For ANI1x the main text and App. A.3 give 32 radial basis functions while the App. A.3 interaction MLP maps 64; 32 is encoded.
# - The ethanol-in-vacuum architecture settings are not stated beyond the output modules; its dipole, polarisability and shielding errors are not energies or forces and are not encoded.
# - The model timed in Table 6 is not identified beyond '1L' and '2L'; per-atom times are the per-molecule times divided by the atom counts.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/simeon2023.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

